    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Description\n\nPlease forgive me if I'm just not smart enough to configure mini.surround on my own.\r\n\r\nBut can someone help me out with how to configure the plugin to surround the text of a paragraph and exclude trailing whitespace? I add two spaces at the end of my paragraphs for purposes of Markdown, so when I try to surround a paragraph, for instance, with quotation marks, the ending quotation mark is placed after those two trailing spaces instead of up against the period at the end of the paragraph.\r\n\r\nIf for some reason this is not configurable, then I would think that pretty much everyone would like to see this. However, I'm pretty sure I just can't understand how to configure the existing plugin. I find the documentation to be particularly difficult to understand or even obtuse, but maybe it's just me.\r\n\r\nThanks in advance.",
