        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Thanks!\r\n\r\nI'm sorry to say though that after updating to the latest version, I still don't know how to create and/or execute a command that will surround a single paragraph while excluding trailing spaces so that the surround character at the end is up against the text rather than being placed after a space or two.\r\n\r\nI'd be happy to use the appropriate \"paragraph without trailing whitespace\" textobject (instead of ip) to do this, but I'm a bit lost. I'm sure it's in the documentation, but the concepts involved here haven't penetrated my skull yet. And when you say, \"For example, created with 'mini.ai',\" I really don't know what you mean there.\r\n\r\nIt appears that you have implemented what you call \"a special handling of trailing whitespace at the last line\", but again I'm pretty well lost as to how to use it. I do realize that I should read the documentation, but as I said, I'm having a little trouble with grokking the concepts. Any help would be appreciated.\r\n\r\nI would also like to mention that I've observed that `mini.surround` seems to interpret multiple paragraphs not separated by a blank line as being all one paragraph. When I say multiple paragraphs, I mean blocks of text terminated by a newline character appearing one after the other in my document. Whereas, `mini.surround` seems to interpret a paragraph as meaning two newline characters after a block of text rather than just one.\r\n\r\nThanks again.",
