        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I'm sorry to say though that after updating to the latest version, I still don't know how to create and/or execute a command that will surround a single paragraph while excluding trailing spaces so that the surround character at the end is up against the text rather than being placed after a space or two.\r\n\r\nWhat did you try? It should work with `saip` followed by surrounding identifier, same as you mention in the title.\r\n\r\nHere is a screencast (red background highlights trailing whitespace and comes from 'mini.trailspace'):\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b314c751-b841-46c5-a477-509629636aad\r\n\r\n> I would also like to mention that I've observed that `mini.surround` seems to interpret multiple paragraphs not separated by a blank line as being all one paragraph.\r\n\r\nThis is not 'mini.surround' that does this, but Neovim itself. See `:h ip` and `:h paragraph`.",
